    "corrective_alternative": "none",
    "notice_days": 2,
    "serious_injury_recall": false,
    "quote": "A recall is mandatory when any model exceeds 8 thermal incidents per 100,000 installed units in a year. Within 24 hours of determining that the threshold has been exceeded, the manufacturer shall notify the regulator; within 48 hours, it shall notify affected customers, stop sales of that model, and provide interim safety instructions pending regulator-approved corrective action."
   }
